From: Aurélien Pommel <aurelien.pommel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: retry a read ended by a cleared halt

When the host clears a bulk endpoint's halt, dwc3 gives the read queued on
it back with EPIPE. adbd took that for a dead link and closed functionfs,
which unbinds the gadget; usb-gadget-adb bound it again, the host opened
it again, and adb never connected. adb 37 on macOS does this on every
open with its default USB backend. Nothing was received, so read again.
---
--- a/core/adbd/usb_linux_client.c
+++ b/core/adbd/usb_linux_client.c
@@ -385,11 +385,15 @@
 static int bulk_read(int bulk_out, char *buf, size_t length)
 {
     size_t count = 0;
+    int stalls = 0;
     int ret;

     do {
         ret = adb_read(bulk_out, buf + count, length - count);
         if (ret < 0) {
+            /* dwc3 ends a queued read with EPIPE when the host clears the halt. */
+            if (errno == EPIPE && count == 0 && stalls++ < 8)
+                continue;
             if (errno != EINTR) {
                 D("[ bulk_read failed fd=%d length=%d count=%d ]\n",
                                            bulk_out, length, count);
